            <ArticleTitle>[13-Year old boy with abdominal pain].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>A3566</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 13-year old boy presents with pain in the lower right abdomen, showing clinical signs of appendicitis. During McBurney' incision an appendix sana was seen. Histologic examination showed penetrating enterobiasis. This was treated with mebendazol.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
